A compact formalization is $\begin{aligned}
T_t &\approx E_t^{\mathrm{op}},\\
E_t^{\mathrm{cap}} &\text{ may be financed by } \Delta B_t>0.\end{aligned}$ Here $T_t$ is current tax revenue, $E_t^{\mathrm{op}}$ operating expenditure, $E_t^{\mathrm{cap}}$ capital expenditure, and $B_t$ debt. The balanced-budget discipline applies to current operations, not to the entire intertemporal plan of the jurisdiction.

